From: jfacemyer <1776340+jfacemyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:29:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Keep screen coordinates in WM_MOUSEHWHEEL and
 never make it a non-client message.

Both wheel messages carry the pointer position in screen coordinates and
Windows has no non-client wheel message, but process_mouse_message()
exempted only WM_MOUSEWHEEL from the conversion. WM_MOUSEHWHEEL arrived
with client coordinates over the client area and, over the frame, as
message 0xae with the hit-test code in wParam, which applications ignore.

From neutron-wine (Nico-LaFoucate).
---
 dlls/win32u/message.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/message.c b/dlls/win32u/message.c
index 0a2f5d1..869330a 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -2725,7 +2725,7 @@ static BOOL process_mouse_message( MSG *msg, UINT hw_id, ULONG_PTR extra_info, H
     message = msg->message;
     wparam = msg->wParam;
     /* Note: windows has no concept of a non-client wheel message */
-    if (message != WM_MOUSEWHEEL)
+    if (message != WM_MOUSEWHEEL && message != WM_MOUSEHWHEEL)
     {
         if (hittest != HTCLIENT)
         {
